# Applies to any build whose context is the repository root, which today
# means apps/api - it needs packages/shared as well as its own directory, and
# a single context covering both is the only shape that works on a platform
# that does not expose Docker's named build contexts. Render's dockerContext
# is singular, so the additional_contexts trick docker-compose used cannot
# survive a deploy there.
#
# Without this file, a root context sends the entire repository to the
# daemon, which on this project is hundreds of megabytes of node_modules and
# git history that the API image has no use for.

.git
.gitignore

# Never in an image. The API reads its configuration from the environment the
# platform provides; baking a local .env in would ship development secrets
# into a deployed artefact.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

**/node_modules
**/.next
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.mypy_cache

# Test and build artefacts.
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/.playwright
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
